X:1
T:Nocturne Op. 37 No. 1
C:Frédéric Chopin
O:Nocturne in G minor, Op. 37 No. 1
N:The first two sections (16 bars): the opening theme and the contrasting theme.
N:The reprise and the chorale that follows are left out. Transposed down a fourth
N:from G minor to D minor, so the lowest note is C#4 and the highest F5. Notes from
N:two Humdrum first-edition encodings (ifdo.ca, kern2abc) that agree. Left out: the
N:grace-note groups before several beats, and the inner notes of the chords in
N:bars 7 and 8. The trill in bar 8 is marked T. The last bar stops after three
N:beats, where the next pass's pickup D (tied to the first note) comes in. Chords
N:simplified from the left hand.
M:4/4
Q:1/4=56
L:1/8
